  "remaining": [
    "screen-space selection, named selection sets, layer grouping and stroke merging",
    "morph symmetry and DNA behavior migration after hierarchy/scale edits",
    "semantic sliders and macrodetails interpolation",
    "eyes, oral assets, textures, hair, runtime morph followers and production garment collision/fitting",
    "tangent, secondary UV/color fidelity and external-app authored normal/identity retention",
    "production MetaHuman DNA ML/RBF/twist/swing data and actual application integration",
    "actual CC5/Unreal generation, animation and detailed re-editing",
    "Windows/Linux execution and large-template performance",
    "actual external-application edited-rig reexport with scale profile restoration",
    "nonuniform bind-scale application interchange and source joint-frame retention"
  ],
  "limits": [
    "surface brush distance is an original-edge graph approximation, not an exact continuous geodesic",
    "point masks do not mask UV, joint, material or record identity metadata",
    "validation garment is a rough CC0 body-derived proxy, not production cloth",
    "actual Blender import validates rest/skin numerics, not production visual character quality",
    "one stable root at bone ID zero; changing source bone counts/IDs remains a separate operation",
    "TRS cannot represent every local shear created by reparenting or child preservation",
    "parent overrides are discrete whenever an active layer has positive weight",
    "original DNA behavior tables cannot yet migrate to edited hierarchy or nonunit bind scale",
    "Blender importer retargets its internal base mesh; application geometry is checked against original exported file positions",
    "human application position tolerance is 0.1 millimetres; small analytic fixture tolerance is 2 micrometres",
    "unit bind-scale normalization requires locally uniform source bind scales and preserves the original project plus explicit scale profile"
  ],
